WEBVTT

00:09.000 --> 00:10.119
Turn right.

00:14.679 --> 00:16.519
<i>The hallway just ahead</i>
<i>has your way out.</i>

00:16.920 --> 00:20.359
<i>I'm cutting the power now. The barrier</i>
<i>will be open for five seconds.</i>

00:28.800 --> 00:29.719
Zai.

00:31.000 --> 00:32.039
Higan.

02:08.599 --> 02:09.560
Zai.

02:13.240 --> 02:14.400
Mari is dead.

02:15.199 --> 02:17.199
Did the order come from Yamaji?

02:18.080 --> 02:22.520
Those who tried to cheat death
still remain in its shadow.

02:23.840 --> 02:25.360
You will die.

02:26.439 --> 02:27.360
Zai!

02:33.120 --> 02:36.400
This doesn't seem like the kind of place
where an ex-AUZA employee would live.

02:36.879 --> 02:40.080
- Are you absolutely sure he's here?
- That's definitely the place.

02:40.960 --> 02:43.280
<i>The guy didn't accomplish much</i>
<i>during his tenure there,</i>

02:43.360 --> 02:47.000
<i>so he wasn't highly regarded</i>
<i>as a researcher or anything like that.</i>

02:47.400 --> 02:50.000
<i>But considering he went out of his way</i>
<i>to find a hiding spot,</i>

02:50.080 --> 02:51.879
you'd think he'd know something, right?

02:51.960 --> 02:55.120
If this turns out to be a bust,
I expect you to dig up another lead.

02:55.199 --> 02:56.560
Remember, I treated you to dinner.

02:57.240 --> 02:59.560
<i>Of course.</i>
<i>And then you'll treat me to another one.</i>

03:00.680 --> 03:02.800
<i>Anyway, it's a safe bet</i>
<i>that the FBI's top brass</i>

03:02.879 --> 03:04.159
have started keeping tabs on you.

03:04.759 --> 03:07.599
<i>So only contact me</i>
<i>in case of emergencies from now on.</i>

03:07.680 --> 03:10.879
- Yeah, okay.
- Alright. Good luck.

03:20.439 --> 03:22.599
Got any games that aren't busted?

03:26.520 --> 03:28.240
Who the hell are you?

03:28.319 --> 03:31.000
You must be Jason Cardenas.

03:33.319 --> 03:37.199
An error in the system caused
the barrier to go down for five seconds.

03:38.000 --> 03:42.520
His lack of hesitation most likely
suggests that this was all premeditated.

03:42.599 --> 03:44.719
And what do you think
caused this error?

03:44.800 --> 03:48.159
Still being analyzed. I suspect
he may have had help on the inside.

03:48.479 --> 03:50.439
Who gives a crap about that?

03:51.080 --> 03:52.759
Let's stick it to him real hard

03:53.759 --> 03:56.520
and show all the exiled
what they have in store.

03:56.840 --> 03:58.439
Our plans won't change.

03:58.520 --> 04:00.719
Higan's secret art
will remain hidden for now.

04:01.199 --> 04:03.159
It would be foolish
to attack him carelessly.

04:03.680 --> 04:06.199
Well, then, how about this for a plan?

04:07.560 --> 04:09.560
We just let him into the city.

04:10.120 --> 04:11.919
All of our forces are here.

04:12.000 --> 04:15.599
His secret art won't mean shit
if he gets beaten to a bloody pulp.

04:16.120 --> 04:18.600
Fighting him in the city
is too high of a risk.

04:18.680 --> 04:21.439
Any collateral damage
will reflect poorly on AUZA.

04:21.519 --> 04:23.959
And who's to blame
for that security error?

04:24.040 --> 04:26.360
Come on now.
What's with all this squabbling?

04:26.439 --> 04:30.199
Personally, I like it.
I don't mind taking the blame for it all.

04:30.839 --> 04:33.879
Very well. Shall we lead him
to the test room at headquarters?

04:33.959 --> 04:35.319
That's perfect.

04:35.399 --> 04:38.639
Fighting against him is gonna provide us
with the best data ever.

04:42.920 --> 04:44.240
I have some news.

04:44.720 --> 04:48.160
<i>It seems the organization</i>
<i>has decided to let you into the city.</i>

04:48.480 --> 04:49.920
It's a trap, obviously.

04:50.639 --> 04:53.879
<i>They are deploying highly skilled ninjas</i>
<i>to eliminate you.</i>

04:53.959 --> 04:56.759
<i>You will almost certainly die</i>
<i>if you fight them.</i>

04:56.839 --> 04:57.879
Don't fall for it.

04:57.959 --> 04:59.519
It's too late. I'm going in.

05:00.040 --> 05:04.519
I'm going to kill Yamaji and make sure
everyone else gets what they deserve.

05:05.120 --> 05:06.560
That's why I came here.

05:06.920 --> 05:08.639
This may be the only chance I get.

05:10.759 --> 05:12.279
Make your move at 7:00 p.m.

05:12.639 --> 05:15.199
<i>The city has planned a parade</i>
<i>to start at that time</i>

05:15.279 --> 05:17.600
<i>as camouflage</i>
<i>for their fight against you.</i>

05:18.879 --> 05:20.480
I wish you the best.

05:22.600 --> 05:24.279
So, what's it this time?

05:24.360 --> 05:26.959
Did you come to rat me out
to AUZA for more money?

05:27.040 --> 05:30.759
Look, I ain't gonna do that. I just need
your help with my investigation.

05:31.160 --> 05:34.120
So tell me what you know, then I'll
leave you alone, like I was never here.

05:34.639 --> 05:37.279
Nobody should have been able
to figure out who I was.

05:37.360 --> 05:38.920
Did I not use enough layers?

05:39.319 --> 05:42.519
Unless... Could it be the whole protocol
got cracked?

05:42.600 --> 05:44.120
I'm so screwed.

05:44.199 --> 05:47.199
Oh, man.
Now, this game takes me back.

05:47.279 --> 05:49.879
I used to play it all the time
when I was a kid.

05:52.439 --> 05:53.720
Move it out of the way, would ya?

05:59.920 --> 06:01.040
Bingo.

06:01.600 --> 06:04.040
Well, well, what do we have here?

06:08.399 --> 06:11.199
Three, two, one!

07:09.040 --> 07:10.000
Nice.

07:10.600 --> 07:13.079
Looks like you got a huge server room
set up down here

07:13.160 --> 07:14.360
for all your hacking needs.

07:18.399 --> 07:20.079
I'm gonna bring the whole thing down.

07:20.600 --> 07:21.680
I'll end that company.

07:21.759 --> 07:24.319
Those bastards won't get away
with how they treated me.

07:24.399 --> 07:27.680
I won't stand for it.
Voluntary resignation, my ass.

07:28.120 --> 07:30.800
Those scumbags hounded me
into quitting.

07:30.879 --> 07:32.639
Damn them, damn them,
damn them all to hell!

07:32.720 --> 07:35.120
Sounds like a personality
problem to me.

07:35.199 --> 07:38.120
No, it's not! Those pricks were just
envious of me.

07:38.199 --> 07:40.680
And so you set this all up to get revenge?

07:41.319 --> 07:45.600
<i>He wasn't highly regarded</i>
<i>as a researcher or anything like that.</i>

07:45.680 --> 07:47.720
I think you might be wrong about that.

07:47.800 --> 07:52.199
I'm pretty positive that company and their
execs are knee deep in shady business.

07:52.279 --> 07:53.759
But since nobody seems to believe me,

07:53.839 --> 07:56.839
I'm gonna dig up their secrets and put
them out there for the world to see.

07:56.920 --> 07:59.519
Calm down, man.
I believe you.

07:59.959 --> 08:01.959
I want to see you go through with it.

08:02.040 --> 08:04.399
I'm just as interested
in taking them down as you are.

08:05.079 --> 08:07.720
You can hack your way
into their servers, right?

08:07.800 --> 08:12.120
No way. Their security is no joke. I'd be
totally screwed if they were to find--

08:12.199 --> 08:13.439
It's alright.

08:13.959 --> 08:15.399
I'll keep you safe.

09:10.960 --> 09:13.759
Just keep in mind I can't take
down their servers or anything.

09:14.080 --> 09:17.200
Not a problem.
Information is all that we're after here.

09:17.799 --> 09:18.879
Just go for it.

09:25.200 --> 09:27.960
This looks like the Technical
Development Department's server.

09:28.399 --> 09:33.000
Well, now, based on the date, this must
be the most recent research report.

09:33.080 --> 09:35.519
Looks like the stuff they typically
send out to investors.

09:36.120 --> 09:38.600
Nothing special here.
Let's look deeper.

09:39.039 --> 09:40.240
Yeah. Go ahead.

09:40.720 --> 09:43.080
What about this?
It's the system source code.

09:43.639 --> 09:46.159
No, not the kind of data we need.
Try looking elsewhere.

10:04.480 --> 10:05.639
Okay. How about here?

10:06.320 --> 10:07.960
It's one of their
internal network servers.

10:08.559 --> 10:11.039
You'd be surprised what kind of stuff
they leave on these things.

10:11.480 --> 10:12.840
"Bound"?

10:12.919 --> 10:15.679
A list of employees.
Or maybe customer info?

10:16.440 --> 10:19.919
No, those look like
Social Security numbers and prices.

10:20.399 --> 10:22.919
Are they buying up
fake identities or what?

10:23.000 --> 10:25.879
Yeah, that's pretty common
for big companies.

10:25.960 --> 10:27.960
They use them to plant operatives.

10:28.039 --> 10:31.200
"Bound" seems to be the name
of some corporate spy group.

10:31.279 --> 10:32.519
This helps us out a lot.

10:33.200 --> 10:36.480
Oh, yeah, that proves it.
AUZA's corrupt as hell.

10:36.840 --> 10:41.039
But none of this data is about the ninjas,
though. Guess it's never that easy.

10:42.919 --> 10:46.080
Emma?
What's her name doing on this list?

10:46.919 --> 10:48.919
- Is that someone you know?
- Yeah.

10:49.360 --> 10:51.480
It's probably just some person
with the same name.

10:51.559 --> 10:53.480
What the hell does all this mean?

10:57.399 --> 10:58.639
Oh, crap. They're onto us.

10:59.960 --> 11:01.279
AUZA's shutting me out.

11:02.360 --> 11:04.360
And now we've got company!

11:04.799 --> 11:05.879
Friggin' hell.

11:40.919 --> 11:43.480
Guess the FBI must have ratted on me.

11:43.559 --> 11:45.600
Just who the hell were those guys?

11:45.960 --> 11:48.799
Probably some mercenaries
hired by AUZA.

12:26.399 --> 12:28.960
Oh, man. Not my hideout.
Damn!

12:30.039 --> 12:32.080
What the hell is going on?

12:34.919 --> 12:36.559
Crap. They're on our tail.

12:43.360 --> 12:45.240
Can't you drive any faster than this?

12:45.320 --> 12:48.039
This is the fastest
your piece of shit car can go.

12:48.120 --> 12:49.039
Aw, hell!

12:56.919 --> 12:57.960
Damn it.

13:04.679 --> 13:06.000
Hit the brakes now!

13:12.720 --> 13:14.879
Man, you're a real sharpshooter.

13:18.519 --> 13:19.759
Get out of the way now!

13:20.519 --> 13:21.559
Okay!

14:27.320 --> 14:30.480
I've been dreaming about this.
And like I imagined,

14:30.919 --> 14:33.919
looking at your ass makes me
all hot and bothered.

14:34.000 --> 14:36.480
I'm impressed you made it up this far.

14:36.960 --> 14:38.039
Okay, now.

14:39.000 --> 14:40.679
Let's see what you've got.

14:41.639 --> 14:42.879
Start the test.

14:52.320 --> 14:53.639
Yamaji...

14:56.240 --> 14:57.440
Yamaji!

15:23.960 --> 15:27.360
Oh, please. Those old ninja tricks
of yours are so outdated.

15:34.759 --> 15:36.279
Yamaji!

16:04.840 --> 16:05.960
I love you.

16:07.799 --> 16:09.240
Any second now...

16:13.120 --> 16:16.480
Never do it again.
It will kill you next time.

16:16.960 --> 16:18.759
...we will all be together soon.

16:30.759 --> 16:32.960
This is the moment I've been waiting for.

16:33.039 --> 16:36.559
Come on.
Let me hear your cute little squeals.

16:49.600 --> 16:51.440
There you are.

17:14.599 --> 17:17.920
The quiet lake gleams
in the morning sun.

17:33.720 --> 17:35.279
Sorry for the interruption,

17:35.359 --> 17:38.359
but he's supposed to be my bitch!

17:45.480 --> 17:46.880
Nice pass.

17:49.200 --> 17:51.240
This is a boring fight.

17:59.880 --> 18:01.960
Are we finished already?

18:19.720 --> 18:20.759
Do you get it now?

18:21.920 --> 18:25.119
The path to hell that you were on
is inescapable.

18:28.880 --> 18:30.039
Yamaji...

18:43.759 --> 18:45.359
Yamaji...

18:46.640 --> 18:48.039
Yamaji...

19:01.680 --> 19:03.599
Let us end this here and now.

20:42.119 --> 20:47.039
Subtitling
FAST TITLES MEDIA
